{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat >> collab/yang-clojure/1794671000001-d1-bounds-declaration-draft.md <<'EOF'\n\n### r13 completed static C1 comparison — pilot only\n\n\"'`1794735000000-engineer-d1-r12-static-c1-pilot.edn` now records 155\npre-declaration passes, no refusals or pending fixtures (SHA-256\n`2cfca729308e1544ccc1c60ccce768ef8f52950816ddf0767132352dafd50b4b`).\nThe final continuation opened the retained store in 281,890 ms and sampled\n3,944,340,192 bytes process used heap at 5 ms, including opening. The first\n20 outcomes were recorded by earlier processes; the interrupted earlier\nbatch did not record a final heap peak. The largest marker relation was\n12,085 rows and 6,493,504 canonical-CBOR bytes, maxima independently taken.\nAcross all outcomes cold maxima in ms were baseline tree publish/load\n3,532/1,865, projection 4,413, marker derivation 17,453, C1 publish/load\n5,883/2,492, relation build 7 and query 1,938. Repeated-call maxima were\n2,548/865, 2,880, 16,308, 6,406/3,294, 5 and 1,371 respectively.\nThese maxima can come from different fixtures and processes, and are not\nadditive. The full per-fixture samples remain in the progress file.\n\nEach comparison reconstructs markers from the retained before tree and\nadmission origin, compares supplied metadata, and checks the same root and\nmarker address on a second call. All 155 pairs agree. Each call uses separate\nbaseline and C1 in-memory stores; the second reuses those stores and the JVM.\nThe process does not execute a guest, produce instruction provenance, publish\nan index, or reconstruct the frontend/compiler/recipe. These labels do not\nmean independent cold JVMs or complete S/B configurations. Used-heap sampling\ncan miss peaks, includes allocations unrelated to any one fixture, and is not\nprocess RSS or exclusive retained memory. This measurement supplies neither\ncomplete B/S/T provenance nor enforceable limits, and